# Quality Gates Hardening
# Scope: linting tool config (E501, ruff line-length) and type checker selection (basedpyright).
# For file/coverage/security limits, see quality-gates.mdc.
RULE: E501 enforced (line-length 120). Use basedpyright (not pyright/mypy). Format first, then check --fix.
WHY: Aligns IDE and CI; basedpyright supports reportAny; E501 catches remaining long lines.
CODEX: 06-coding-standards/quality-gates.md
DO: `ruff format --line-length 120`; `timeout 120 basedpyright <source_dir>/`; never add E501 to ignore
NEVER: Use pyright or mypy; add E501 to ruff ignore; skip format before check
See also: quality-gates.mdc (size limits, coverage, security), basedpyright-safety.mdc (execution safety)
